    {
      "page_title": "GiST: A Lossy Search-Tree Framework",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Tree Framework",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "GiST = Generalized Search Tree, a balanced tree framework",
            "The data type supplies the behaviour, not the index",
            "Internal nodes store a lossy summary of their subtree",
            "A search descends every branch whose summary might match"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "btree node",
                "lines": [
                  "disjoint key ranges",
                  "exactly one path down",
                  "exact keys"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "GiST node",
                "lines": [
                  "overlapping summaries",
                  "many paths possible",
                  "lossy bounding keys"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "How Inserts Pick A Path",
          "text": "`union` builds a parent's summary; `penalty` picks the child that grows least; `picksplit` divides a full page."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Range Types"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX ON booking",
            "  USING gist (during);",
            "WHERE during && tstzrange(",
            "  '2026-09-01', '2026-09-02');"
          ],
          "note": "&& = overlaps, any shared instant"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "GiST in Practice & SP-GiST Partitioning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lossy summaries make results approximate",
            "Every candidate row is rechecked against the heap",
            "Unlike btree, subtree regions may overlap",
            "Search follows multiple paths, so worst case is data-dependent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What It Indexes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Operators"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "PostGIS `geometry`",
              "`&&`, `<->`, ST_Intersects"
            ],
            [
              "`tstzrange`, `int4range`",
              "`@>`, `&&`, `<<`, `>>`"
            ],
            [
              "text `gist_trgm_ops`",
              "`LIKE '%x%'`"
            ],
            [
              "`point`",
              "`<->` nearest neighbour"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Exclusion Constraints"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE EXTENSION btree_gist;",
            "ALTER TABLE booking ADD EXCLUDE USING gist",
            "  (room WITH =, during WITH &&);",
            "-- no double-booking; btree cannot do this"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`btree_gist` lets scalar types join a GiST index",
            "So an equality column sits beside a range column",
            "Both live in one exclusion constraint"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Nearest Neighbour"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT name FROM places",
            "ORDER BY loc <-> point '(0,0)'",
            "LIMIT 10;  -- ordered GiST scan",
            "-- no full sort of the table"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`gist_trgm_ops` is smaller and faster to build than GIN",
            "But slower to search, so GIN wins read-heavy text",
            "GiST updates are cheaper than GIN's",
            "Prefer GiST when the column is written often"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SP-GiST"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Space-Partitioned GiST: unbalanced, non-overlapping partitions",
            "Quadtrees, k-d trees and radix tries",
            "Excels at point data and `inet` addresses",
            "Also text prefix search, where partitions never overlap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX ON hosts USING",
            "  spgist (ip);  -- inet_ops",
            "WHERE ip << '10.0.0.0/8';",
            "CREATE INDEX ON t USING",
            "  spgist (name);",
            "WHERE name ^@ 'abc'; -- prefix"
          ],
          "note": "^@ is the starts-with operator"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`<<` = ==contained within== a subnet",
            "Radix trie shares prefixes, so text keys stay compact",
            "Partitions never overlap, so one path down"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Index",
            "Search",
            "Build",
            "Size"
          ],
